# Copy this file to .env and fill in values — NEVER commit .env
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  STEP 1 — TRUST THE SAP ROOT CERTIFICATE (one-time setup per machine)
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  If your SAP system uses an internal/corporate TLS certificate, Node.js will
#  reject it by default with "unable to get local issuer certificate".
#
#  1. Open the SAP system URL in Chrome/Edge → padlock icon → "Certificate is
#     valid" → Details → select the ROOT certificate (topmost in the chain)
#     → Export → Base-64 encoded X.509 (.pem)
#  2. Save it to: C:\Users\<you>\.claude\sap-root-ca.pem
#  3. Set it as a permanent Windows User env var (run once in PowerShell):
#       [System.Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable(
#         "NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS",
#         "C:\Users\<you>\.claude\sap-root-ca.pem",
#         "User"
#       )
#  4. Open a NEW terminal for it to take effect.
#
#  Do NOT set NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS in this .env file — dotenv loads too late
#  for Node's TLS initialisation to pick it up.
#
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  STEP 2 — SAP LOGON CREDENTIALS (Basic Auth — user + password)
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  Preferred: store them once in Windows Credential Manager instead of here:
#    cmdkey /add:PO_MCP /user:<SAP_USER> /pass:<SAP_PASSWORD>
#
#  Or, less secure, set them directly below:
SAP_USER=
SAP_PASSWORD=

# Optional: override the Windows Credential Manager target name
# SAP_CRED_TARGET=PO_MCP

#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  STEP 3 — CONNECTION SETTINGS
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
SAP_BASE_URL=https://<host>:<port>
SAP_CLIENT=<3-digit client number>

#  Full OData V4 service root path (everything after the host:port, up to and
#  including the trailing slash). The metadata namespace is
#  "com.sap.gateway.srvd.zpru_purcorderhdr_odata.v0001", but the actual URL
#  segment depends on how the service was published (SICF/SEGW/RAP service
#  binding) and cannot be derived from the metadata file alone.
#
#  Typical RAP V4 pattern:
#    /sap/opu/odata4/sap/<service-binding-name>/srvd/sap/zpru_purcorderhdr_odata/0001/
#
#  Find it via:
#    - SAP Fiori Launchpad → the app's "About" dialog, or
#    - transaction /IWFND/V4_ADMIN or /n/IWFND/MAINT_SERVICE, or
#    - ask Basis / the service owner for the exact service binding path
#
SAP_SERVICE_PATH=/sap/opu/odata4/sap/<service-binding-name>/srvd/sap/zpru_purcorderhdr_odata/0001/
